Wireshark Filters
=================

DISPLAY FILTERS
---------------

Purpose                         Filter
Show HTTP                       http
Show DNS                        dns
Show TCP                        tcp
Show UDP                        udp
Show ICMP                       icmp
Specific IP                    ip.addr == 192.168.1.10
Source IP                      ip.src == 192.168.1.10
Destination IP                 ip.dst == 192.168.1.10
Specific port                  tcp.port == 80
Source port                   tcp.srcport == 443
Destination port              tcp.dstport == 80
Combine conditions             ip.addr == 192.168.1.10 && tcp
Either condition               dns || http
Exclude traffic                !arp
HTTP GET requests              http.request.method == "GET"
TCP SYN packets                tcp.flags.syn == 1 && tcp.flags.ack == 0


CAPTURE FILTERS
---------------

Purpose                         Filter
Specific host                  host 192.168.1.10
Source host                    src host 192.168.1.10
Destination host               dst host 192.168.1.10
Specific port                  port 80
TCP port                       tcp port 443
Network                        net 192.168.1.0/24


NOTE
----
Display filters and capture filters use different syntax.

Example:
Display filter:  tcp.port == 80
Capture filter:  tcp port 80
